---
// Rebuilt from the live WordPress page layout.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BunnyVideo from '../components/BunnyVideo.astro';
---

<Layout title="Kids Party Watchables - clamcentral.com">
	<main class="px-4 pt-12 pb-20" style="background: #fffdf4">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-[1080px]">
			<div>
				<h1 style="font-size:clamp(31px, 3.21vw, 45px);line-height:1.30;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700"><strong>Kids Party Watchables</strong></h1>
				<h3 style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.71vw, 24px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700"><strong>Windows computer crowd games!</strong></h3>
			</div>
			<div style="margin-top:20px">
				<BunnyVideo src="https://vz-541977fa-fc1.b-cdn.net/ff85ec7e-f54e-4792-b2ba-c958836a7aa1/playlist.m3u8" poster="https://vz-541977fa-fc1.b-cdn.net/ff85ec7e-f54e-4792-b2ba-c958836a7aa1/thumbnail.jpg" width="568" />
			</div>
			<div style="margin-top:55px">
				<h2 style="font-size:clamp(23px, 2.43vw, 34px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700"><strong>What are KIDS PARTY WATCHABLES?<br /></strong></h2>
			</div>
			<div style="margin-top:21px">
				<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
					<li style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left">Lightweight, super easy to operate Windows games to show on a wall screen.</li>
					<li style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left">The kids always play as teams with the event leader totally in control of the game.</li>
					<li style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left">Launch and play within seconds even by leaders that have never experienced a Watchable.</li>
					<li style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left">No game playing skills are required. The games are played by the computer. The teacher uses the keyboard to step a game forward as needed.</li>
					<li style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left">With a wireless keyboard, the teacher can control the game from anywhere in the room. All instructions for the teacher (such as which keys to press) are always on screen in each game.</li>
					<li style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left">No mouse is needed, except to simply launch KP Watchables 1 itself.</li>
					<li style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left">Download and installation is simple and quick.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
			<div style="margin-top:26px">
				<h2 style="font-size:clamp(23px, 2.43vw, 34px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700"><strong><strong>KP Watchables' Points-Earning Games</strong></strong></h2>
				<h3 style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.71vw, 24px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700"><strong><strong>And by games we mean KIDS PARTY-style extra-fun games.</strong></strong></h3>
			</div>
			<div style="margin-top:1px">
				<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.60;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:center"><strong>These wild games are designed to get kids and teams earning the all-important KP Points as fast as possible! Running a KIDS PARTY event on a Friday Night is a blast - you can turn down the lights, fire up the screen, start a game and COVER YOUR EARS because the mob starts screaming and jumping! A veritable Eighth Wonder of the World!</strong></p>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/kp-ball.webp" alt="" width="674" height="378" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>KP Ball!</strong> When it’s time for your KIDS PARTY kids to relax and take a breather, turn down the lights if it’s dark outside and run this incredible game. The kids will go NUTS watching their teams rack up the points! Can be easily set for two, three or four teams. Really adds excitement to your KIDS PARTY or typical fun events. KP Ball games last 2½ minutes.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/races.webp" alt="" width="674" height="378" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>At the Races!</strong> Teams earn points if they correctly predict the winning car. This one gets them shouting! Play several rapid-fire rounds: Each race lasts for about ten seconds or less. Teams can switch cars or not after each race. You'll need someone to add up the number of races each team wins.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/pizza-toss.webp" alt="" width="674" height="379" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>Pizza Toss.</strong> The team that catches the pizza wins points. Or use this fun game to choose a team randomly. Can be set for two, three or four teams. Eliminate teams you don’t have, then play.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/kp-bingo.webp" alt="" width="674" height="378" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>KP Points Bingo.</strong> No matter how many KP teams you’re running, have them choose up sides for this two-team game. The winning team (or teams) gets all the KP Bingo points. If you wish, you can keep playing until the other side also scores a Bingo. A huge number of possible outcomes. You will literally never play the same game twice in a lifetime of playing!</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/kp-name-game.webp" alt="" width="674" height="378" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>The Name Game.</strong> Your regular attendees will rack up points starting from the very first KP event. But what about new kids who start late? This game helps them to immediately earn points for themselves and their teams. Points are awarded when the adult leader types in a newcomer’s name. Like all the games, the points are shuffled each time you play. In this case, if you have two or more kids with the same name, the points value will likely be different for each one. Kinda neat!</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/10x.webp" alt="" width="674" height="378" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>10x.</strong> Use this game to multiply the number of points kids earn when you draw names from a container. Kids choose a letter for you to click. Multipliers range from 2x to 10x. A player that starts with 1000 points can multiply that up to 10,000 points. And remember, players that earn points earn the same amount for their teams!</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/kp-points.webp" alt="" width="674" height="378" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>Doorski!</strong> Draw somebody’s name from a hat and let them indicate which number door for you to click. Instant points for that kid and his or her team. Super quick, you can play it several times in a row. The two smaller balloons show the points behind doors not chosen. It doesn't matter if players pick the same door multiple times in a row, the points are always randomized from 0000 to 9999.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-6 md:flex-row md:items-start md:justify-center" style="margin-top:70px">
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:337px">
					<img src="/images/pages/squeal.webp" alt="" width="674" height="378" loading="lazy" class="mx-auto h-auto w-full" style="max-width:337px" />
				</div>
				<div class="w-full" style="max-width:686px">
					<p style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.40;color:rgb(0, 0, 0);text-align:left;max-width:686px;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto"><strong>Squeal or No Squeal!</strong> A great way to end KIDS PARTY events, and saves the set-up time required by the paper version found in the Kids Party resources Wallgames 1 and Wallgames 2. This is the one exception to the rule that KP Watchables games require practically no time or the adult leaders to learn. This one you need to understand before you start it up for the kids. Happily, the rules are on the first screen of Squeal or No Squeal.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div style="margin-top:51px">
				<h3 style="font-size:clamp(18px, 1.71vw, 24px);line-height:1.40;color:rgb(12, 17, 21);text-align:center;font-weight:700"><strong><strong>Kids Party Watchables 1 comes with the Kids Party Program</strong></strong></h3>
			</div>
			<div style="margin-top:20px">
				<div class="text-center"><a href="/kids-party-events-program/" class="inline-block w-full rounded-[5px] px-[18px] py-3 font-button text-[18px] font-bold tracking-[2px] text-white hover:opacity-85" style="max-width:434px;background:rgb(19, 92, 164)">Go to the Kids Party Program page</a></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>
